cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the associated article and this
  software version.
type: software
title: >-
  glorys-antarctic-correction: adaptive thermodynamic correction of GLORYS12V1
  profiles against CTD casts in Marguerite Bay, Antarctic Peninsula
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Gabo2000s/glorys-antarctic-correction"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  MATLAB and Python implementations of an adaptive thermodynamic correction
  of GLORYS12V1 temperature and salinity profiles against CTD observations.
  The correction combines a depth-weighted bias term and a
  stratification-weighted structural term, with an adjustment in the
  diffusive-convection regime identified by the Turner angle, using TEOS-10.
  Both implementations give the same results. Includes six CTD casts from
  Marguerite Bay, Antarctic Peninsula (December 2025), the corresponding
  GLORYS12V1 profiles, and the corrected profiles and metrics.
